<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panamanian Defense Forces</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1983–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Panama Defence Forces</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Panamanian Defense Forces were Panama's armed forces from 1983 to 1989, formed when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a> was reorganised into a combined army, navy, air force and police under the command of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>. They were the real centre of power, controlling the state and much of the economy. They were destroyed by the American invasion of December 1989, and a standing army was abolished in 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panamanian-defense-forces.jpg" alt="Panamanian Defense Forces" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG-image-maker · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Panama_(1925-1941,_1946-2006).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
